{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>You shall not kindle.</b> Since he mentioned, regarding the first day and the seventh of the Festival of Unleavened Bread, that no manner of work shall be done in them (above 12:16), yet permitted food for the soul, he now says regarding the Sabbath: you shall not kindle fire—to bake bread and to cook meat, for fire is needed for every food. And the Gaon [Saadia] composed a valued book of replies against those who dispute our predecessors regarding the Sabbath lamp."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:40:29.733419274Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}